  "strategy": "The proposed approach is a gradient-based optimization using a multi-subproblem strategy. Beginning from a uniform distribution, the algorithm identifies critical convolution points (where the maximum occurs) and refines the sequence structure by adjusting coefficients based on extreme points in the constraint space. \n\nKey phases include:\n1. Evaluation Setup: Handles security and preliminary checks while initializing the best candidate.\n2. Core Optimization: Uses an adaptive Markov decision process (MDP) with heuristic-based rule selection and priority scheduling.\n3. Fine-Tuning: Iterative polishing focusing on minimizing the non-convex objective via multiple restarts.\n\nThe solution features aggressive dimension reduction, clever use of sse4.2 and avx2 instruction optimizations, and a dynamic hyperparameter handover system. By prioritizing sub-outcomes - separating convolution contributions, aggressive coefficient reduction, and structured restarts - the implementation efficiently closes in on the global minimum while remaining within hardware execution constraints.",
